# Rule: /trinny-london

A client pitch page built as a HOMEPAGE VARIANT on the ADR-053 recipe, forced
into light, unlisted. Same `LandingPage`, same corridor, order
hero → about → the Arc → the proof casefile (+ the ring) → contact.

**Read first**

- [ADR-093](../../sentinel/decisions/093-trinny-london-light-locked-variant.md) — this route
- [ADR-053](../../sentinel/decisions/053-workshop-corridor-variant.md) — the recipe it repeats, and its two invariants
- [ADR-058](../../sentinel/decisions/058-light-mode-theme.md) — the theme channel the lock overrides
- [ADR-059](../../sentinel/decisions/059-rail-instruments.md) — the four-corner scheme and its two clocks

## Contracts

- **Variant-local CSS only.** `trinny-london.css` is scoped to `.tl-root` (or
  keyed on `<html>`, for chrome the wrapper cannot reach). Never port a rule
  from it into `landing.css` / `home-v2.css` / `services.css` /
  `rail-instruments.css` — a shared-sheet edit changes `/` and
  `/claude-workshop`. ⚠ ADR-053's two rules are DUPLICATED here rather than
  shared: one rule scoped to both roots is a shared sheet by another name.
- ⚠ **THE LOCK NEVER WRITES `localStorage`.** `data-theme` is a paint decision;
  `tf-theme` is the visitor's. A lock that persisted itself would follow the
  reader back to `/`. It also beats `?theme=dark` — a pitch page has no
  legitimate dark reading, and the smoke asks for dark to prove it.
- ⚠ **STAMPING THE ATTRIBUTE IS HALF THE JOB.** `ThemeLock` calls
  `hydrateFromDom()` immediately after, because the WebGL painters and the
  services drawer's bake read the STORE, not the attribute
  ([`services-ring.md`](services-ring.md) records the drawer half). And it is a
  `useLayoutEffect`: a passive one lands after `HeroThemeGlitch` subscribes, and
  the notify then reads as a real flip and warms both hero plates (~780 kB) on a
  page that can never toggle.
- ⚠ **A ROUTE EARNS ITS `LIGHT_LOCKED_ROUTES` ROW AND ITS `HERO_ROUTES` ROW BY
  HAND.** Both lists are hand-written; nothing derives them, so nothing else
  would say a route had changed its theme or its plate. A locked route also
  needs the rule that hides the switch — a lock without it leaves a control that
  visibly does nothing.
- ⚠ **THE ROSTER IS BUILT FROM THE PAGE ORDER, NEVER FROM PRODUCTION CLOCKS.**
  `markState` compares indices, so a production mark carries its production
  position: reordering `JOURNEY_MARKS` makes About read `ahead` at the offer and
  Thesis `passed` inside the bio, with every mark rendering and nothing throwing.
  `TRINNY_JOURNEY_ORDER` is the one clock; changing the page's sections means
  editing that array and nothing else.
- ⚠ **AND THE SECTOR TOTAL IS PART OF THE ROSTER.** It shipped as `01/07` on a
  five-row page: the hook seeded production's total and its bail-out compared
  only the POSITION, which at rest on the hero is 0 either way. Any new state on
  that hook is compared in the same check.
- **`resolveActiveIdx`'s `preMountStationId` defaults to `hero`** and must stay
  byte-identical for `/`. On this page the lag station is `about`, because the
  corridor mount is not a `.station`.
- **The nav items are a PROP.** They are hardcoded in React, so the parse-time
  link cleanup cannot reach them; filtering at mount instead would flash the
  dead links on the hero and change the drawer's count after hydration.
- **The workshop's guard stays untouched.** `claude-workshop-parse.test.ts`
  pins its own prototype; this route has `trinny-london-parse.test.ts`. The two
  HTML files are byte-identical at the fork and will diverge — only the PATH
  check can tell them apart until then.
- **The page is unlisted:** `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`, absent
  from `app/sitemap.ts`. ⚠ The forked prototype under `/prototypes/` deploys and
  is world-fetchable (robots-disallowed only) — the same exposure class, worth
  remembering when client copy lands in it.
- ⚠ **ADR-100: `#proposition` mounts the `board` kind** — `ArcBoard` over
  `TRINNY_BOARD` (same slot, same `id: "configuration"`): the client's
  configuration as two svg drawings, the proof's R4 grammar at page scale, no
  frame, no picker, server-only. ⚠ U2 (owner, 2026-09-14) is the live cut: a
  ruled LEDGER of four facts beside the assembled BOARD — they may not mirror
  each other. The gold chip is `AI CAPABILITY` / "owned by the team"; four
  tools are peers; no diamonds; THE CONTEXT, not THE LAYER. ⚠ U3 (same day):
  the LEDGER arrives slower (0.72s / 140ms against the board's 0.42 / 80), and
  every LIT rung is scoped `[data-board-state="configured"]` or the ladder is
  dead — `animation:` resets `animation-delay`, which U1 shipped unnoticed.
  ⚠ The turn's paragraph is the one line on this page allowed
  "self-sufficient" (ADR-095 U8, owner) and `.tl-turn__sub` is 52ch so the
  word does not break at its own hyphen; its TITLE binds the client's name
  with a NO-BREAK SPACE, and the house decode kernel had to learn U+00A0 is
  whitespace (it resolves to ITSELF, never to a plain space).
  ⚠ ADR-099 U1: `.tl-root .hero__content` takes `margin-inline:
var(--rail-inset)` so the hero seats on ADR-048's editorial band like
  `#about` and all nine proposal heads — 192 against 360 at 1920×1247, and
  IDENTICAL below the band's crossover, which is why only his own viewport
  showed it. Join the band; never re-inset the sections.
  ⚠ ADR-098 U5: the three phase plates keep the TOP-RIGHT notch only — the
  bottom-left one bit the inverse foot's own text. The record is the discovery call in roles; `trinny-offer.test.ts`
  and `arc-board-fit.test.ts` walk it. Canonical text:
  `.claude/rules/trinny-london.md` and `.claude/rules/arcs.md`.
- ⚠ **ADR-101 §A: BOTH BEATS STRIKE IN, SEATED, AND NOTHING RISES** (owner,
  2026-09-14: the next section's elements _"don't have to fly in … they need to
  have a glitch effect like we have on our homepage"_, only once the turn has
  emptied). It is the PROOF CARD's strike-in (ADR-097 U11) copied as
  `tl-glitch-*`, never the hero's canvas slice-tear — that one samples the
  painted page, which has nothing to sample until the thing is visible.
  ⚠ `--tl-prop-lead` 50svh → **100svh**, so `p` and `q` saturate on ONE frame
  and `#proposition`'s top IS the turn's release; `TURN_PROP_VEIL_IN` 0 →
  0.384 and `_FULL` 0.5 → 1 move with it or the two clocks race on the mark's
  one-owner veil. ⚠ The trigger is a HYSTERESIS (`arriveNext`, pure) and
  `await` is not `out`. ⚠ `PROP_ARRIVE_IN` is **0.99, not 1**: `propArrival`
  clamps, so 1 needs top ≤ 0 exactly and every roller lands at 0.22px with the
  record hidden — a threshold no measurement can rest on fires by luck.
  ⚠ `t` joins the writer's delta gate (p and q agree for the whole of
  `#offer`'s scroll) and `#phases` is resolved in `measure()` + a
  `ResizeObserver`, because `#offer` is a lazy root and a query in the effect
  body returns null forever. ⚠ Taking ADR-100's ladder away takes its resting
  paint with it (board opacity 0, ribbons undrawn) — both restored
  route-scoped. ⚠ Delays ride `var(--tl-gl-d)` INSIDE the shorthand, fill
  `backwards`. ⚠ An absent stamp means SHOWN. Canonical text:
  `.claude/rules/trinny-london.md` §The two strike-ins.
- ⚠ **ADR-101 §B: THE CHIP BECOMES THE THREE PLATE HEAD BANDS** (owner: it
  _"moves into the center of the screen, and then it copies itself left and
  right … I don't want fucking cross-dissolves"_). ⚠ ONE MATERIAL, so there
  is nothing to cross-fade: `--arc-gold-wash` on `.arc-root`, aliased by the
  board, painted by the plate's head AND its foot — which retires ADR-098
  U2's inverse DELIVERABLE band house-wide. ⚠ One summed expression over
  three windows (detach / split / seat), never a branch, with `chip` and
  `head` read LIVE every frame: the two welds measure 0.00px on all four
  terms. ⚠ The layer is ABSOLUTE in document space on `document.body`, never
  fixed — a fixed carrier is composited against the viewport, so a missed
  frame unglues it from the two things it is welding. ⚠ The chip is hidden
  and its OUTLINE is not (four ribbons still meet that box; what stays is the
  socket). ⚠ Every token resolved through a PROBE, and a `display: none`
  layer measures ZERO — the baseline probe read 0 and dropped the words
  18.85px with nothing erroring. ⚠ `rollToT` converges on the BEAT'S RECT:
  `seamProgress` clamps, so a `t = 0` target on the published clock arrives
  two viewports short. Canonical text: `.claude/rules/trinny-london.md`
  §The seam.
- ⚠ **ADR-102: `#proposition` IS ONE PINNED SCENE, AND IT RETIRES §A.3 AND
  §B.1–B.3 ABOVE** (owner, same day: the flight "jitters and lags", starts
  "almost immediately", and the cards must "collapse inwards so it feels like
  one configuration" before anything moves). The slot is a sticky stage that
  pins on the frame the record strikes in; the PHASES beat renders INSIDE it
  over the board (`TRINNY_SCENE`; `#offer` opens on the flow); everything from
  the dwell to the paragraph is a pure function of `sv`, the station's clock in
  VIEWPORT UNITS (dwell 0–40 · withdraw 40–70 · fold 58–109 · hand-over 112 ·
  slide 114–150 · title 134–164 · unrolls 152–274 with the two copies between ·
  paragraph 278–302 · runway 325svh). ⚠ The jitter was a main-thread writer
  against a compositor scroll; the carrier lives INSIDE the stage now, welded
  to things that do not move (0.00px of stage motion under the wheel). ⚠ The
  layout is keyed on the writer's `data-tl-scene` stamp and FAILS OPEN; the
  ground's canvas is sticky and viewport-sized (the ground's `overflow: hidden`
  had to go); `data-tl-scene-past` is a LATCH cleared only when the record
  strikes out; the nodes SHRINK before they travel (tools and reach paint over
  the chip); the seat lane retracts with the opposite dash sign; a copy holds
  its source's words until it has separated. ⚠ Four silent traps: drain the
  `MutationObserver` after every measure (the probes mutate what it watches);
  a `ResizeObserver` on a fixed-height stage is blind; a React root's first
  render clears its container (mount the layer from `measure()`); `-top / vh`
  at the pin is `-0`. ⚠ The plates' feet ran 23.7px past the stage at
  1280×720 with the beat's "one viewport" read green (the beat's box IS the
  stage); a bottom-pad trim changed nothing (content flows from the top), so
  under `(max-height: 760px)` both heads in the scene take the terminal cut's
  `clamp(28px, 5.5vh, 72px)` and the smoke measures the FEET against the
  stage. Canonical text: `.claude/rules/trinny-london.md` §The scene; the
  record is ADR-102.
- ⚠ **ADR-103 (2026-09-15, owner: the eyebrow "disappears" while the title
  and paragraph "always appear at the same location" — "morph it via a glitch
  effect"; and a third beat, "what you actually get", NOT the phases
  restated): THE HEAD DECODES IN PLACE, AND THE PLATES BECOME THE
  DELIVERABLES.** The head NEVER CLOSES — ADR-102's withdraw keeps only the
  ledger svg, the four head-column apertures are deleted, and a second layer
  in the stage (`headCarrier.ts`, the seam's idiom with zero travel) holds one
  leaf per RENDERED LINE of each head run (a `Range` walked word by word,
  grouped by line, the half-leading taken off), scrambling the chrome and the
  title and TYPING the paragraph as ONE typewriter; the real text is hidden
  per beat by `data-tl-head-lead` / `-intro` on the columns' CHILDREN, never
  the column. Windows `[[1.34,1.64],[3.34,3.64]]` / `[[2.78,3.02],[4.12,4.36]]`.
  Then `#outcomes` (`TRINNY_OUTCOMES`, the `steps` kind, the fifth exception)
  inside the same scene: COLLAPSE 3.24–3.64 (LIFO, `unrollY` back to the
  band) · STACK carriers 3/4/5 3.68–4.10 (band i → row i; the rows ARE plate
  heads, one material) · STEPS from 4.40 at `SCENE_STEP_SPAN` 0.5 (the one
  dial), a 0.16 crossover, the open row filled and the rest ring-only, each
  stage a centre-out aperture on its own `stepProgress` clock · `SCENE_END`
  5.98 · runway **605svh**. The first stage is a computer-vision SCAN of the
  packshot (`ArcScanVisual`: a gold edge sweeping the image over its grey
  ghost, 1px div leaders to labels on their own bed, the checks the grading
  gates); stages 2 and 3 are framed fields. Every channel has a FINISHED
  default (PRM / no-JS read whole). ⚠ Traps: the observer filters BOTH
  layers; the rows are measured whole then COLLAPSED before the seam reads
  the landing boxes; the seam guard reads `headCarrier.ts` as text (say
  "document-space scroll offset", never the literal); two 8px fixes collide
  over a 200px field (container query); `SCENE_SETTLED` is 5.95 and
  `SCENE_PHASES_SETTLED` 3.1. Canonical text: `.claude/rules/trinny-london.md`
  §The head decodes; the record is ADR-103.

